   "limitations": "The death's fades only cover the backgrounds and the backdrop (the sprites, projectiles, particles and HUD are not drawn in SUB_GAME_MODE_DYING, as natively); the haze reset of COLOR_FADING_TO_BLACK is not reproduced. The head is processed with ProcessMenuOam instead of ProcessComplexMenuOam (it is never rotated or scaled). The continue leaves one frame earlier (unk_75c04 runs in the same frame). Without a saved file the continue restarts the runtime's starting state (the room and equipment the runtime started with), not the native new-file start. The debug variant and the demo ending are not ported. Not compared with an emulator. \"When the hit kills Samus (SUB_GAME_MODE_DYING) the sprites, projectiles and HUD stop and vanish, the room fades to black in 8 frames (gMonochromeBgFading, COLOR_FADING_TO_BLACK) and its backgrounds switch off; at the dying animation's first flash the backdrop fades to white (COLOR_FADING_TO_WHITE), with Samus alone in front. When SamusDying's timer reaches 120 the runtime opens the game over screen on the native screen PPU: GameOverInit loads its palette, the file select icons, the background and text tile tables, the graphics and the English \"\"try again\"\" prompt from the ROM bank, stops the sounds and fades from white (BLDY 16 down to 2, then the window and darkening up to 6) before the game over music. The GAME OVER letters breathe (sGameOverTextGradientPaletteOffset every 20 frames). UP and DOWN choose between \"\"yes (return to game)\"\" and \"\"no (to title screen)\"\" with Samus's head, the text palettes and the WIN1 window following, with the menu sounds; A or START plays the start sound and the head's animation, then the screen darkens to black with the music fading. Yes loads the most recent save file (Samus in the save platform's tube) or restarts the game's start; no leads to the intro (GM_INTRO), then the title. Checked by capture in norfair_022 (death in the lava with --energy 2, the menu, both answers).\"",
