   "limitations": "Not compared with an emulator. The unknown item block's explosion, the morph ball launcher, the ziplines, their buttons, the generator's electricity, the pistons and the glass tube keep the sprites' priority instead of their BG priority (bgPriority); event and hard-mode spritesets are not resolved, so a gadget only placed by them (brinstar_000's elevator pad) does not appear. The zipline's EU-only gSamusPhysics.horizontalMovingDirection update is not applied (USA build) and the grab does not move gPreviousYPosition. The glass tube's break was only checked in tests (no capture: it needs the Fully Powered Suit's event). The pillar's second dust particles are drawn at the normal priority instead of behind BG1. The AIs follow the decompilation: the elevator pad (moved 2 pixels up, always active, synced to Samus and on its Moving animation while she uses an elevator); water drops (hidden for gSpriteRng * 8 frames, spawning animation, falling by sSpritesFallingSpeed, splashing on a block with SpriteUtilCheckVerticalCollisionAtPositionSlopes or on the water surface held at gEffectYPosition, hidden again for 100 + rng * 8 frames at a random x offset); steam (ground, ceiling with Y flip one block up, left or right wall turned horizontal, killed in the air; large/small draw distances; a random first frame; the large or small steam sound on screen at frame 0); diagonal steam (X flip without a wall on its left, Y flip for the downward ones); Gerons (their event checks, three CAA_MAKE_NON_POWER_GRIP blocks, shaking on ISFT 2 with its sound, the destroyed stump after their event; the destruction and its events when four Parasites hold one) and the Norfair Geron (gone after EVENT_POWER_GRIP_OBTAINED); unknown item blocks (2x2 CAA_MAKE_SOLID_GRIPPABLE blocks, ignoring projectiles until their item event, then destroyed by a hit: CAA_REMOVE_SOLID, the breaking sound, the light secondary at frame 7). Checked by capture in crateria_001 (steam), brinstar_021 (Geron), kraid_012 (Space Jump block) and crateria_011 (Plasma Beam block, water drops). Morph ball launchers: their back part and the five blocks around made non power grip; a bomb in its first spin set on the launcher is taken (BOMB_STAGE_PLACED_ON_LAUNCHER), the launcher waits half a second and plays its launching animation, and when the bomb's explosion launches Samus (SPOSE_DELAY_BEFORE_BALLSPARKING) the energy appears around her for a second. Checked by capture in brinstar_000 (the launch is stopped by the power bomb blocks above, as natively before the Power Bombs). Ziplines: the initial direction away from the stop-enemy block beside them, Samus grabbed from below (SSC_ZIPLINE), the grabbing, grabbed and releasing animations (unlit, then lit once EVENT_ZIPLINES_ACTIVATED is set), the run to the other stop-enemy block once lit (a quarter block a frame, a pixel less carrying Samus, the moving sound every 16 frames and its fade), the snap to the block's middle that drops her (SPOSE_MID_AIR_REQUEST) and the turn; zipline buttons (two blocks up, bound to the room's zipline or removed, lit with the event, a shot calls the zipline with its sound, active until it stops); the zipline generator (its conductor behind Samus, four CAA_MAKE_SOLID_GRIPPABLE blocks, Samus in morph ball at its top set to SPOSE_ACTIVATING_ZIPLINES for two seconds with the activating sound, the morph symbol over her, the electricity at 1.5 seconds, the animated palette back on at 16 frames from the end, then the event and SPOSE_MORPH_BALL; already activated after the event). Checked by capture in kraid_004 (activation, the button shot from the generator, the zipline's run from 440 to 232 and its turn, Samus hanging under it). Pistons: four body blocks made non power grip, the bottom one once Samus is away, a damaging beam or bomb hit on the head (ISFT_DAMAGED) opens them with their sound, freeing the bottom block on the opening's third frame, then the top block once Samus is out of it; checked by capture in brinstar_028 (a standing shot from the right raises the piston). The glass tube: intact (with the rain sound before the Fully Powered Suit), a power bomb touching it after that suit sets EVENT_GLASS_TUBE_BROKEN, two seconds later it cracks with its sound, then opens its two rows of eleven blocks with dust at its four ends and a half-second shake both ways, and stays broken (its rows removed at once on later visits); the intact tube was checked by capture in chozodia_023. Before this patch the gadget OAM tables past the 72nd (the ziplines' and gates') overflowed MzmSpriteKind and read zero durations; the limit is now 128 with static asserts. The rising Chozo pillar (crateria_016 and crateria_017): never drawn, it waits for EVENT_POWER_GRIP_OBTAINED, then for 704 frames raises BG2 (gBg2Movement.yOffset, half a pixel a frame) with its sound, a vertical shake every 32 frames and the ROM's debris and dust patterns, spawns its three shadowed, two and one plain platforms over three frames (two CAA_MAKE_SOLID_GRIPPABLE blocks each, the spawning sound and animation, the shadow behind Samus on the 22nd frame), and sets EVENT_CHOZO_PILLAR_FULLY_EXTENDED; later visits place the platforms at once. Checked by capture in crateria_016 with --event 16 (the pillar rising, then the platforms appearing). Gerons in their idle state catch every Parasite whose point is inside them (the Parasite's collision cleared so it counts once); four destroy them; checked by capture in brinstar_023 (VARIA3 destroyed, VARIA1 getting destroyed).",
