   "limitations": "The banner is kept outside the sprite slots and is drawn centred in the wider runtime view (the GBA position 120, 54 offset by the view's extra 32 rows); it always loads its graphics (no spriteset holds it); the escape start and the item acquisition pause screen are not ported; the English text is the only language exported. The exporter transliterates TextProcessMessageBanner, TextProcessCurrentMessage and TextDrawMessageCharacter on the banner's OBJ VRAM (sMessageBannerGfx, color 15 fill, glyphs of sCharactersGfx with sCharacterWidths, eight characters a frame, the US line overflow) for every English message of sMessageTextPointers, renders the banner's six OAM tables with each message, and records the TextProcessMessageBanner calls each message takes. The runtime runs MessageBanner frame by frame: the nine graphics frames, the text processing with the animation held, the shown banner (items and first tanks back up player 2 and insert the item or unknown item jingle; the fully powered suit plays the Brinstar remix behind its jingle; tank messages back up player 2, play the tank jingle and retrieve player 2 at removal; maps and save complete play the tank jingle; one-line tables for items, first tanks, maps, save complete and the fully powered suit), 100 static frames before A, B or a direction closes it, the removal animation, gPreventMovementTimer held at SAMUS_ITEM_PMT meanwhile (SamusUpdate skipped, sprites stopped except uninitialized ones, no Samus contact); its removal finishes a tank collection, and the end of an item message's text (stage 3 of the text processing) runs BgClipFinishCollectingAbility, which registers the ability in gItemsCollected and on the minimap. Once removed, the banner keeps its last pose, as its sprite slot does natively, for the map station that waits for MESSAGE_BANNER_POSE_REMOVAL_ANIMATION. The save prompt spawns its YES/NO cursor (SaveYesNoCursor, drawn at its absolute position shifted like the banner): LEFT and RIGHT move it with their sound, A answers (work1), NO plays the refusal and closes the banner, YES hides the cursor and saves on its next update (MZM_BANNER_SAVE); the save complete message re-enables the pause when it goes.",
