   "limitations": "the transition probes run every frame for doors, the tank probes on odd frames only. On odd frames, the four probes of BgClipCheckTouchingTransitionOrTank (Samus's right and left hitbox edges on her center row, the bottom and top rows on her center column) read the behaviors of the current Clipdata, last probe first; a revealed tank (hidden ones are not tanks until their block breaks) on an explored minimap tile (MinimapCheckIsTileExplored) starts gCollectingTank, sets gPreventMovementTimer, raises the equipment within the game total (sStartingHealthAmmo, the total of sNumberOfTanksPerArea and sTankIncreaseAmount, exported from the decompilation: 100 energy refilled, 5 missiles, 2 super missiles, 2 power bombs) and spawns the message banner (the first missile, super missile or power bomb tank with its own message). BgClipFinishCollectingTank (on the banner's removal) empties the BG1 block, clears the Clipdata to air or water (underwater tanks) and registers the item in gItemsCollected by area and room and on the minimap (MinimapUpdateForCollectedItem); BgClipRemoveCollectedTanks removes them again on every room load. Checked in brinstar_019 (`--spawn 615 96`, Right): Samus walks onto the energy tank column, energy 99 to 199, the banner shows its two lines and Samus stays frozen until A; the tank block is then empty. The tank increases follow the game's difficulty (sTankIncreaseAmount[gDifficulty]: 100/5/2/2 on easy and normal, 50/2/1/1 on hard), exported per difficulty.",
