   "limitations": "The Stop syscall (SYSCALL 3 with the keypad interrupt on SELECT, L and R) is reproduced as a sleeping state: the runtime stops presenting the screen (black, the LCD being off) and pauses the audio device instead of SoundBias0; the game keeps polling the keys each frame. gDisableSoftReset is not modeled (no soft reset exists). The English text is always used. Not compared with an emulator. \"L on the map screen plays the opening sound and runs PauseScreenEasySleepInit: the map fades out by four BLDALPHA levels a frame, the L prompt and the visor overlays change, the easy sleep tilemap replaces the map overlay and the equipment names graphics are backed up and replaced by the text, drawn a few steps a frame in the mask mode (TextDrawEasySleep with TextProcessCurrentMessage and TextDrawMessageCharacter: \"\"Activate Easy Sleep?\"\" and the SELECT, L and R hint, plus the YES/NO prompt drawn by TextDrawYesNoEasySleep at PauseScreenInit), then it fades in with the cursor on NO. LEFT and RIGHT move the cursor with their sound, A on NO refuses, B, L or R closes (PauseScreenQuitEasySleep restores the overlay and the graphics); A on YES waits half a second, blanks the screen and sleeps until SELECT, L and R are held, then waits for every key to be released with the cursor back on NO. Checked by capture in brinstar_000.\"",
