   "limitations": "BG1 and BG2 show screens 24 and 23, which this mode never loads: the game's leftover VRAM there is not kept (the screen PPU is cleared). The game's fade into the pause is not played and the music is not lowered (as in the game, only START lowers it). The HUD minimap is redrawn and transferred over the next frames instead of the HUD graphics reload of the return to the game. The unused instant download types 1 and 2 are not ported. Not compared with an emulator. With PAUSE_SCREEN_MAP_DOWNLOAD, PauseScreenInit flags the screen as on the map and downloading, keeps the explored map on BG3, marks the area's map downloaded, recomputes gDecompressedMinimapVisitedTiles with the downloaded tiles (PauseScreenGetMinimapData, MinimapSetDownloadedTiles), uses the download BG layout (the visor on BG0 at the highest priority, BG3 with the mosaic bit, BG1 scrolled by 4 pixels), shows only the area name (priority 0), Samus's and the boss icons at priority 1 (the boss icon hidden until the line passes it) and no scroll arrows or viewable areas. PauseScreenMapDownload waits 8 frames, starts the line from the BG3 scroll, copies one map row every 8 frames for 21 rows while the line and its four trails move, transfers the whole map, redraws the minimap, removes the line and waits half a second; then A, B or START leaves. Checked by capture in brinstar_032.",
