   "limitations": "The bitmap modes 3 to 5 are not rendered; the window and blending registers are read once per frame (no mid-frame register changes or HBlank effects); the affine backgrounds use the reference point plus the line times PB/PD instead of the latched internal registers; objects beyond 128 per frame, the per-line object cycle limit and the affine object mosaic are not modelled. The ROM bank holds the whole verified ROM (private, never committed). gba_ppu renders the GBA display memories as GBATEK describes them: text backgrounds (four sizes, 16 and 256 colors, flips, scrolling, mosaic), affine backgrounds (wrap, overflow), regular and affine objects (all shapes and sizes, 1D and 2D mapping, flips, double size, semi-transparency, the object window, mosaic), the front-most two layers per pixel by priority, window 0, window 1, the object window and the outside, alpha blending, brightness up and down, and forced blank. scripts/mzm_rom_bank.py copies the verified ROM into a private bank and lists the 14462 sized data objects of the reference ELF (name, GBA address, size); mzm_rom looks them up by name and reads them by address, and decompresses the BIOS LZ77 and run-length streams.",
